# Tracer: a function-valued set family preserves its member carrier through
# multiple checked `have fn` definitions.

have fn row(x N+) power_set(cart(N+, N+)) = {point cart(N+, N+): point[1] = x}
have fn rows(n N+) fn(K N+) power_set(cart(N+, N+)) = fn(x N+) power_set(cart(N+, N+)) {row(x)}

# Before (did not work):
# forall n, K N+, point rows(n)(K):
#     point[1] $in N+
# Former behavior: well-definedness stopped after unfolding `rows(n)(K)` to
# `row(K)` and reported `index target point is not a tuple`.

# Now (verified):
forall n, K N+, point rows(n)(K):
    point[1] $in N+
# Current behavior: bounded unfolding reaches row(K)'s checked set builder, so
# membership supplies the declared cart(N+, N+) carrier and its first projection.
# Boundary: a family returning power_set(N+) does not make its members tuples;
# the executable Rust regression still rejects indexing such a member.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/03_language_features/function_valued_set_family_carrier.lit
# Implementation: src/runtime/runtime_known_object_properties.rs and membership inference/verification.
